as 5. Contract [1], for 14,988 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The data shows that some contracts are just under the limit, but it doesn't prove any wrongdoing. Prices may be low, budgets fixed, or needs separate. Statistical trends don't indicate improper actions by the body or contractors.\nWhat can be checked: Check the dates and amounts of the December contracts to see if they fit a pattern. Review awardee A's contracts to see if they repeat the same need. Look at contract [1] to see what was purchased and how it fits the December trend.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["%2FAnDaQyDmCd9PLkba5eRog%3D%3D","7JgPagBMg5j%2B3JAijKO%2Bkg%3D%3D","k%2F5zpjFqnb%2F%2Fa9DgO%2BoYKQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}